id: pm-elmpav
title: "Refusal reachability: every error code declares the states it owns, and an entrypoint-level probe proves each state is still reachable as that typed code rather than as an untyped fault"
description: ""
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 1
tags[8]: agent-ux,"area:ci","area:contracts","area:sdk",error-taxonomy,gate,measurement,reachability
created_at: "2026-08-10T06:09:23.711Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-10T06:09:48.075Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 900
acceptance_criteria: "Each error code in the generated catalog may declare the observable states it owns and the entrypoints through which each state is reachable; A probe drives a real command entrypoint into each declared state and asserts the refusal carries the declared code and exit class; A declared state with no reachable entrypoint fails CI rather than passing silently; A state that surfaces as an unclassified runtime error fails CI with the same finding; The declaration set may start empty and grow one code at a time, constraining nothing until a state is declared"
value: Turns the error-code catalog from an inventory of codes the product can emit into a falsifiable claim that each code is still produced by the pipeline agents actually run.
impact: "Closes the only defect class in this repository that is invisible to both unit tests and coverage: a correct guard stranded behind a newly added upstream read."
outcome: An owned state with no reachable entrypoint is a CI finding; a state reachable only as an untyped fault is the same finding from the other side.
why_now: "pm-6xlyss is a measured instance. tracker_root_not_directory was complete, typed, and unit-tested, yet the state it guards reached production as an unclassified fault and blocked the daily release for a full window."
parent: pm-33cw
risk: medium
confidence: medium
